# 13. Batch Job Statuses

Batch job different statuses mein ja sakta hai:

```text
Holding
   ↓
Queued
   ↓
Preparing
   ↓
Processing
   ↓
Completed
```

Agar problem ho:

```text
Failed
```

Ya manually stop karo:

```text
Aborted
```

### Meaning

| Status     | Simple Meaning                |
| ---------- | ----------------------------- |
| Holding    | Flex Queue mein wait kar raha |
| Queued     | Run hone ka wait              |
| Preparing  | `start()` execute ho raha     |
| Processing | `execute()` chal raha         |
| Completed  | Job finish                    |
| Failed     | System failure                |
| Aborted    | User ne stop kiya             |

---

# 14. Apex Flex Queue

Ye thoda confusing topic hai.

Suppose tumne 10 Batch jobs submit kiye:

```text
Batch A
Batch B
Batch C
Batch D
Batch E
Batch F
Batch G
...
```

Salesforce sabko immediately execute nahi karta.

Flex Queue mein jobs:

```text
Holding
```

status mein wait kar sakti hain.

Flex Queue mein maximum:

```text
100 Holding jobs
```

ho sakte hain.

Aur Salesforce resources available hone par jobs ko processing queue mein move karta hai.

---

# 15. 5 batch jobs wala limit

Important interview point ⭐

Salesforce ek org mein maximum:

```text
5 queued/active batch jobs
```

simultaneously process/queue state mein allow karta hai as described in the documentation.

Flex Queue enabled hone par additional submitted jobs `Holding` mein wait kar sakti hain, up to the flex-queue limit.

So distinction yaad rakho:

```text
Flex Queue → up to 100 Holding jobs

Queued + Active → up to 5
```

---

# 16. Batch Apex ko trigger se call karna risky kyun hai?

Suppose trigger:

```apex
trigger AccountTrigger on Account (...) {

    Database.executeBatch(new MyBatch());
}
```

Problem?

Trigger bulk mein execute ho sakta hai.

Suppose API se:

```text
10,000 Accounts update
```

ho rahe hain.

Trigger multiple records ke context mein execute ho sakta hai aur repeatedly batch enqueue karne ki koshish kar sakta hai.

Result:

```text
Too many batch jobs
```

ya limit exception.

### Simple rule:

> **Trigger se Batch Apex call karne se pehle ensure karo ki ek transaction multiple batch jobs enqueue na kare.**

Usually trigger se asynchronous processing chahiye ho toh architecture carefully design karna zaroori hai.

---

# 17. Batch Apex mein Callout

Agar Batch Apex ke andar external API call karni hai:

```text
Salesforce
    ↓
HTTP Callout
    ↓
External System
```

Toh class mein:

```apex
Database.AllowsCallouts
```

implement karna hota hai.

Example:

```apex
public class MyBatch
    implements Database.Batchable<Account>,
               Database.AllowsCallouts {
}
```

Then `execute()` mein HTTP callout kar sakte ho.

---

# 18. `Database.Stateful` — Very Important ⭐

Normally har `execute()` separate transaction hai.

Suppose:

```text
Batch 1 → 200 records
Batch 2 → 200 records
Batch 3 → 200 records
```

Agar tum variable mein count rakhte ho:

```apex
Integer count = 0;
```

toh normal Batch Apex mein transaction ke across state maintain nahi hoti.

Agar tum chahte ho:

```text
Batch 1 → count = 200
Batch 2 → count = 400
Batch 3 → count = 600
```

toh:

```apex
Database.Stateful
```

use karo.

Example:

```apex
public class MyBatch
    implements Database.Batchable<Account>,
               Database.Stateful {

    Integer count = 0;

    public void execute(
        Database.BatchableContext bc,
        List<Account> scope
    ) {
        count += scope.size();
    }

    public void finish(Database.BatchableContext bc) {
        System.debug(count);
    }
}
```

### Simple definition:

> `Database.Stateful` = execute transactions ke beech **instance variable ki value preserve karna**.

---

# 19. Static variables ka kya?

Ye important trap hai.

`Database.Stateful` ke saath:

```text
Instance variables → retain state

Static variables → retain nahi karte
```

Example:

```apex
Integer count;       // state retain ho sakti hai

static Integer count; // reset ho jayega
```

