# 20. Batch Apex Testing ⭐

Batch Apex asynchronous hota hai.

Isliye test mein:

```apex
Test.startTest();

Database.executeBatch(
    new MyBatch(),
    200
);

Test.stopTest();
```

use karte hain.

`stopTest()` tak Salesforce asynchronous processing ko test context mein complete kar deta hai, jiske baad results assert kar sakte ho.

---

# 21. Important Testing Rule

Salesforce test framework mein Batch Apex ke liye:

> **Test mein sirf one execution of `execute()` test kiya ja sakta hai.**

Isliye test data aur scope carefully choose karo.

Example:

```apex
200 Accounts
```

aur:

```apex
Database.executeBatch(batch, 200);
```

Then:

```text
1 execute()
```

test ho jayega.

---

# 22. `startTest()` / `stopTest()` ka flow

```apex
Test.startTest();

Database.executeBatch(batch, 200);

Test.stopTest();

// Assertions
System.assertEquals(...);
```

Conceptually:

```text
Test.startTest()
      ↓
Batch enqueue
      ↓
Test.stopTest()
      ↓
Async batch executes
      ↓
Assertions
```

---

# 23. Batch Apex chaining

Batch ke `finish()` se next batch start kar sakte ho.

Example:

```apex
public void finish(Database.BatchableContext bc) {

    Database.executeBatch(new SecondBatch());
}
```

Flow:

```text
Batch 1
   ↓
finish()
   ↓
Batch 2
   ↓
finish()
   ↓
Batch 3
```

Isko:

> **Batch Chaining**

kehte hain.

Benefit:

> Next batch tab start hota hai jab previous batch complete ho chuka ho.

---

# 24. `System.scheduleBatch()`

Agar batch ko future mein ek specific delay ke baad run karna hai:

```apex
System.scheduleBatch(
    new MyBatch(),
    'My Batch Job',
    60
);
```

Meaning approximately:

```text
60 minutes ke baad batch start hone ke liye schedule
```

Important:

> Exact execution time system resources ki availability par depend kar sakta hai.

---

# 25. Batch Apex vs Queueable Apex

Simple difference:

| Batch Apex                           | Queueable Apex                          |
| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------- |
| Large number of records              | Smaller async jobs                      |
| Thousands/millions records           | Complex async processing                |
| `start/execute/finish`               | `execute()`                             |
| Batch processing                     | Single async job                        |
| QueryLocator available               | No QueryLocator                         |
| Stateful possible                    | Different state/chaining model          |
| Large data processing ke liye useful | General async processing ke liye useful |

Simple rule:

```text
Millions of records → Batch Apex

One complex asynchronous task → Queueable Apex
```

